Mutant: rollback-skips-nested
Kind: bug
Class: lifecycle
Configs: rel, dbg
Until: 2.2.1
Version-note: 2.2.2 rewrote this code (the patch is for the 2.2.0/2.2.1 SystemsRunner)
Expect: RUNNER-ROLLBACK-MISSING-DESTROY, RUNNER-INITIALIZED-STATE, RUNNER-ROLLBACK-ORDER
Why: the Init rollback does not destroy nested runners whose Init completed

diff --git a/KenseiECS/Systems/SystemsRunner.cs b/KenseiECS/Systems/SystemsRunner.cs
--- a/KenseiECS/Systems/SystemsRunner.cs
+++ b/KenseiECS/Systems/SystemsRunner.cs
@@ -657,7 +657,7 @@
         // itself uninitialized by then, so the systems after it would never be destroyed.
         private static void DestroyCollecting(IDestroySystem system, World world, ref List<Exception> errors) {
             if (system is SystemsRunner nested) {
-                if (!nested._initialized) {
+                if (nested != null) {
                     return;
                 }
                 nested._initialized = false;
